WEBVTT

00:00:00.520 --> 00:00:03.720
Digital artifacts feel concrete, but they still need context.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:07.830
A screenshot, log excerpt, alert, file name, message header, ticket note,

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:11.300
or threat intelligence indicator may be useful evidence, yet each one is also

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.880
a representation of something else.

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:17.050
It may be filtered, cropped, transformed, copied, exported, summarized,

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:19.045
or separated from surrounding events.

00:00:19.045 --> 00:00:23.170
Counter-deception asks how the artifact was collected and what it can actually prove.

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:24.790
Provenance should be captured early.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:28.150
Analysts should record the source system, collector, collection time, time range,

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:31.126
query or view used, and any transformation applied.

00:00:31.126 --> 00:00:34.810
Timestamps deserve special care because systems may use local time, UTC,

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:37.580
different time zones, clock drift, ingestion delay,

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:39.715
or display formatting that hides precision.

00:00:39.715 --> 00:00:43.580
A timeline built from mixed sources should explain those differences before drawing a

00:00:43.580 --> 00:00:45.040
conclusion from sequence.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:47.215
Screenshots and logs are common sources of confusion.

00:00:47.215 --> 00:00:51.155
A screenshot can preserve useful visual context, but it can omit browser state,

00:00:51.155 --> 00:00:54.380
account context, surrounding messages, or later changes in the system of

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:54.840
record.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:58.725
A log line can confirm that an event was recorded, but it may not explain intent,

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:01.720
user identity, session ownership, or whether related events

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:02.960
were excluded by the query.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.540
The artifact supports only the claim it actually supports.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.745
Where possible, corroborate with independent telemetry or records.

00:01:08.745 --> 00:01:12.915
A suspicious account change might be checked against identity logs, approval tickets,

00:01:12.915 --> 00:01:15.160
device telemetry, and administrator actions.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:18.395
A claimed external indicator might be checked against original reporting,

00:01:18.395 --> 00:01:21.173
internal observations, and relevant time windows.

00:01:21.173 --> 00:01:23.395
Preserve evidence before drawing conclusions,

00:01:23.395 --> 00:01:27.120
maintain chain of custody for sensitive material, and document uncertainty plainly.

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:31.080
Verification is strongest when artifact, context, and decision are tied together.
